                "cache_hit": false,
                "api_called": true,
                "summary": "- The Pomeranian Philharmonic's Symphony Orchestra was formed less than a year after World War II, with roots dating back to the 1930s Municipal Symphony Orchestra in Bydgoszcz.\n- The orchestra has collaborated with notable conductors such as Robert Satanowski, Zbigniew Chwedczuk, Witold Krzemieński, and Antoni Wit.\n- It has performed with renowned conductors and composers like Krzysztof Penderecki, Witold Lutosławski, and Aram Khachaturian.\n- The orchestra has toured internationally, performing in countries such as Germany, France, Italy, and Russia, and has participated in major music festivals.\n- The Pomeranian Philharmonic has commissioned works by Polish composers including Wojciech Kilar, Henryk Mikołaj Górecki, and Romuald Twardowski.\n- The institution is known for its exceptional concert hall with top-tier acoustics and has produced numerous recordings for various labels.",
